  nonce: '8324'  # 8324
  message: "Done. Merged 4ff442c5b0 (PR via auto-pr, CI green). The fix is structural rather than editorial: instead of only correcting the sentence, the scope now lives on MetaKeySpec.applicable_edge_types = frozenset({calls, instantiates}) -- the typed field ADR-0038 ruling 2 already built for per-edge-type applicability. A scope that lives only in prose cannot be checked, which is precisely how this one drifted; a scope in a field can be, and a live-tree producer gate can now assert against the declaration instead of a hand-maintained literal. Also corrected: the ref_construct disambiguation no longer asserts a calls-only scope for its sibling, and records that INV-lajov's 'zero overlap' was a corpus observation promoted to a contract. method_call_recovery._CLASS_HINT_EDGE_TYPES is re-commented to say WHY it holds two values (the analyzers disagree about the dst, INV-kahig) instead of naming which languages take which arm -- the old comment named Java/Kotlin/Python as the calls-fallback languages when java.py and py.py both emit instantiates today and ruby is the one that never does. EVIDENCE. Three new tests in test_axis_meta_keys.py pin the declaration, its canonicality against all_edge_type_names(), and the REASON instantiates is in scope (so a later reader does not tidy it back to one value). Red confirmed before the fix (3 failed on applicable_edge_types is None), green after. Full gated suite: 11872 passed, 1 pre-existing schema-freshness failure resolved by regenerating docs/schema.json, coverage 100%, mypy strict ratchet clean, all 16 pre-commit gates passed. docs/schema.json regenerated -- description-only, 2 lines; NO SCHEMA_VERSION bump, matching the call INV-lajov made for this same key (edge.meta is free-form and no consumer branches on the description)."  # 8324
